{"id":101,"explanation":"Do not cache get_user for the lifetime of a process: after a user's roles are revoked, a cached result could still grant the old roles. #640 is the issue reference for this hazard.","unsure":""}
{"id":102,"explanation":"Check the error returned by db.Query before scheduling rows.Close(). If the query fails, rows is nil and cannot be closed; the shown code returns first.","unsure":""}
{"id":103,"explanation":"The setTimeout call deliberately schedules measure(el) with a zero delay instead of using queueMicrotask, so measurement happens after layout has settled.","unsure":""}
{"id":104,"explanation":"The token has type Secret<String>. Never log its contents; its Debug output is intended to be redacted, so debugging code must not expose the underlying string.","unsure":""}
{"id":105,"explanation":"The RetryCount constant is tied to the Http.Retry setting in appsettings.json. Change both together so the code and configuration agree. appsettings.json is the configuration file; Http.Retry is the setting.","unsure":""}
{"id":106,"explanation":"Before passing offset to ch.map, ensure it is a multiple of pageSize (offset % pageSize = 0). The comment says mmap rejects offsets that are not page aligned.","unsure":""}
{"id":107,"explanation":"The trailing slash in build/ matters to rsync: this command copies the contents of the build directory into $DEST, rather than copying the build directory itself. rsync is the external tool whose path syntax determines that behavior.","unsure":""}
{"id":108,"explanation":"The index on events.created_at uses BRIN for size and workload reasons: the comment says it is 1% of the size of a btree index, and rows are appended in time order. created_at is the indexed column; btree is the comparison index type.","unsure":""}
{"id":109,"explanation":"The loop currently waits by spinning. Replace that wait with a futex; the stated completion condition is that lock_acquire in src/sync/lock.c sleeps while waiting. src/sync/lock.c is the file path, and lock_acquire is the named function.","unsure":""}
{"id":110,"explanation":"The reason dbo.RebuildStats runs on the secondary is documented at the failover section of the runbook. doc:runbook#failover is that documentation anchor; dbo.RebuildStats is the procedure this comment applies to.","unsure":""}
{"id":111,"explanation":"The timeout value of 30 is kept below 60 seconds because an upstream proxy terminates requests that are idle for 60 seconds. The proxy is an external constraint on this timeout.","unsure":""}
{"id":112,"explanation":"Keep Widget's destructor virtual. If it becomes non-virtual, deleting a derived object through a Widget pointer can skip its derived destructor. #915 is the issue reference for this hazard.","unsure":""}
{"id":113,"explanation":"Run PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON before any write on this SQLite connection. The setting applies separately to each connection, so setting it elsewhere does not enable it here.","unsure":""}
{"id":114,"explanation":"The Name field deliberately uses a fixed-length ShortString form, string[40], instead of string because the containing record is written to disk byte for byte. Changing the field type could change its on-disk representation.","unsure":""}
{"id":115,"explanation":"Caller-supplied p_id must be passed as a bound value through :1 and USING p_id. Concatenating that input into the SQL passed to EXECUTE IMMEDIATE would allow SQL injection. :1 is the bind placeholder, and p_id is the caller input.","unsure":""}
